WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.600
Let's embrace...

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.980
Being together like this...

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.900
...is something I'll never forget!

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.310
Forever...

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.830
...under this sky...

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:18.440
...we'll walk together!

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.130
In this beauty...

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:22.240
...that I'm dreaming...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:23.290
...the world's just a...

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.420
...merry, merry-go-round!

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:26.010
With more dreaming...

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:27.080
...and more loving...

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.170
...my heart is a...

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:29.390
...merry, merry-go-round!

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:30.690
Luvly, merry-go-round!

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.080
Getting ready for a good morning...

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.760
...I say 'good morning', then I chat and run.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.940
A lovely life every day...

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.640
...is my wish for you, my sweet heart!

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.740
A, B, C, D, E, F, G!

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:45.390
A lack of vitamins isn't healthy.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.520
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7!

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:50.600
Bring along your favorite and let's go!

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:56.460
Rolling rainbow star!

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:58.830
If you go there...

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.830
...you'll surely find it!

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:06.210
Lovely roller coaster!

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.690
Under this sky...

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.340
...its a total pleasure!

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:16.060
Being together like this...

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.590
...is something I'll never forget!

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:25.780
Under this sky...

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:28.270
...we'll walk together!

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:29.970
Can they stop the Murder Collector?

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:34.270
The job from the famous and elite school, Shibusawa Academy,

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:37.690
was to investigate an unbelievable rumor on the Internet.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:40.770
The rumor was that one of the students at the school.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.650
was filming real murders to make snuff videos

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:50.410
and one of these videos showed the murder of another
student, who had previously been reported as missing

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:55.500
Megu and Ryuu received an order from DDS to infiltrate the school.

00:01:56.310 --> 00:02:00.630
But soon after that, the top student at the school went missing

00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:04.670
and the day after, Megu was kidnapped!

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:08.050
Ryuu searched for her,

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:14.140
but only found a video of them on the Internet,
being broadcast by the criminal.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.440
I-impossible.

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:29.280
Where is that?

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:30.700
You can see the clock tower.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:31.570
Amakusa-kun!

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:45.460
From the angle of the tower,

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:48.050
I'm sure we saw that building, which means...

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:03.480
Hey, this building isn't being used anymore.

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:04.820
No, look.

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:09.190
The boards are old, but those are new nails.

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:11.860
Somebody pulled them out and changed them recently.

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:22.370
This way!

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:26.630
How can you tell?

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:30.840
The other routes are covered with spider webs, but not this one.

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:33.680
That means somebody has been here recently.

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:35.640
Amazing, Amakusa-kun.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:41.770
This is it.

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:43.940
Megu!

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:47.320
Hang on, Megu!

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:51.530
She's alive.

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:52.780
I'm so glad.

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:55.070
Megu, wake up!

00:03:58.850 --> 00:03:59.580
Ryuu-kun.

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:01.370
I'm glad. You're safe.

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:03.420
But...

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:09.760
Kogure.

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:19.930
They were broadcasting the murder over the net?

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:20.890
Yes.

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:22.980
Um, Detective.

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:26.270
There's something about this that bothers me.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:27.770
Who are you?

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:30.690
Asabuki Maya; I was one of the students who found the body.

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:35.660
There's a student in our class, Oobayashi, who's kind of a delinquent type.

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:36.990
I saw him once...

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:43.960
You're telling everybody that I'm the Collector.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.290
Damn you!

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:48.380
Bastard.

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:51.960
He's got to be the one who did it!

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:53.300
And later!

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:56.590
OK, OK. We'll listen to what you have to say later.

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:59.760
Excuse me, Residence Hall Director, Sakuma...

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:01.010
Oh, there you are.

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:05.100
When was the last time you saw Kogure-kun, the victim?

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:07.480
Right after dinner, two days ago.

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.770
I thought he went straight back to his room.

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:12.940
He's got no friends, so he's always like that.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.110
What are you doing?

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:18.370
You can't mess with the crime scene!

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:19.530
Look at this, Detective.

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:24.330
The dust has been wiped away on this desk.

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:25.750
In other words,

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:29.130
this is where the criminal put the camera when he shot the video.

00:05:29.650 --> 00:05:31.500
What of it?

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:33.050
Don't you think it is odd?

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:37.590
Look.

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:39.550
Normally if you shoot from that position,

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:44.390
the light would come in through here and you
would not be able to see the victim's face

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:49.310
But Kogure's face was clearly visible in that footage we saw.

00:05:49.670 --> 00:05:54.280
It's likely the criminal used a portable light, or something, for movie making.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:58.110
He even prepared lighting then.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:05:59.660
Is it just the peculiarities of a pervert?

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:01.910
No, probably not.

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:06.910
The criminal here, isn't just a simple pervert.

00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:12.920
This is more like a pre-meditated act of a very smart person.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:20.010
Um, I'm fine Ryuu-kun.

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:22.470
It's only 7:30.

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:23.890
I'll stay here for a little while longer.

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:27.430
But if somebody sees us like this,

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:29.690
they may get the wrong idea.

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:31.230
That won't happen.

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:34.780
Thanks to that "detective group" you made,

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:36.900
nobody will think it's strange if we are together.

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:39.490
No, that's not what I mean by suspicious...

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:42.030
And I don't think I'll be able to sleep tonight.

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:45.580
Even after a student was killed,

00:06:46.310 --> 00:06:51.290
and you may think this is awful, but I still need to think and ask...

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:52.880
Why?

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:54.960
Explore deeper...

00:06:55.610 --> 00:06:56.300
Stop.

00:06:57.780 --> 00:06:58.630
Ryuu-kun.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:04.760
Yes?

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:06.680
Asabuki-san?

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:08.180
Ah, Ryuu-kun?

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:11.980
There's something about this case that I wanted to show you.

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:13.230
About the case?

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:14.020
Yeah.

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:18.610
I've only been at this school for six months or so,

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:21.740
but I knew Kogure before that.

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:26.620
By which I mean, Kogure went to the middle school that's attached to this one.

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:28.250
So did I.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:32.750
And so did Oobayashi, and Touya, and Tominaga too.

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:34.330
And actually...

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:37.000
Somebody's here.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:38.630
I'll call you back.

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:40.170
Yes?

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:42.340
What?

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:46.810
Asabuki-san hasn't called back.

00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:49.220
Yes?

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:52.770
Touya-san!

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:55.810
Minami-san, I, um...

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:00.940
No, no, you've got it wrong!

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:03.110
We were just talking about the case.

00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:04.030
But...

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:04.820
What's wrong?

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:08.870
I saw a strange message on the BBS.

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:10.410
On the BBS?

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:19.130
“An incredible live broadcast"?

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:21.920
It's almost 9 pm.

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:27.300
This is the same as when Megu was kidnapped.

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:36.560
and sending the footage using a cell-phone and a laptop.

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:49.450
Dammit! Where is that?

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:50.950
Who's room?

00:09:04.570 --> 00:09:05.630
Asabuki-san.

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:08.430
What's going on?

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:09.390
It's late.

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:10.430
Asabuki-san has...

00:09:11.290 --> 00:09:12.390
I'm sorry!

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:16.520
Amakusa-kun, Minami-san, what is this?

00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:18.860
She went to call an ambulance.

00:09:19.210 --> 00:09:20.270
Was it the Collector?

00:09:20.630 --> 00:09:22.480
Why would they attack Asabuki-san?

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:24.450
<i>"Ah, Ryuu-kun?"</i>

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:28.490
<i>"There's something about this case that I wanted to show you."</i>

00:09:28.970 --> 00:09:32.540
<i>If what she was going to show me,</i>

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:34.580
<i>was a hint as to the identity of the criminal...</i>

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:38.170
Megu, have you been in this room before?

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:39.080
Yeah.

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:40.920
Though I just saw a little bit of it.

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:43.880
What has changed since then?

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:45.510
Anything?

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:47.630
Hey, what are you saying?

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:50.350
She just took a quick look at it, she can't remember that.

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:52.930
The way the books are lined up on that shelf, has changed.

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:54.930
No way, you can remember?

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:58.230
I have a photographic memory.

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:00.690
Anything I see, I never forget.

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:03.320
That part has changed a lot.

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:09.700
Videos.

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:12.200
There are a lot.

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:13.950
You guys...

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:15.500
Let's call the police!

00:10:17.270 --> 00:10:18.000
This is strange.

00:10:19.310 --> 00:10:23.090
Tomorrow isn't a day off, but she has her alarm set for 9.

00:10:23.860 --> 00:10:25.710
Classes start at 8.30 though.

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:35.930
What?

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:39.940
Then the criminal broadcast this murder live?

00:10:48.590 --> 00:10:51.660
Asabuki-san liked horror huh?

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:56.500
Um... have you known her for a long time?

00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:57.750
Yes.

00:10:58.140 --> 00:11:01.500
She was in the movie club at the Academy’s middle school...

00:11:01.940 --> 00:11:04.710
I was the advisor there.

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:07.050
Teacher, can you come here for a second?

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:08.090
Yes.

00:11:11.740 --> 00:11:13.930
This video wasn't here a while ago.

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:16.100
Yeah, did somebody put it in?

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:18.680
No, it was probably recording.

00:11:20.460 --> 00:11:22.560
This counter is busted.

00:11:24.550 --> 00:11:25.900
The tape has been totally rewound.

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:27.190
Let's look.

00:11:28.510 --> 00:11:30.030
"So then, here is the problem..."

00:11:31.930 --> 00:11:34.620
It's a quiz program that starts at 8.

00:11:34.970 --> 00:11:36.450
Is this what she was recording?

00:11:36.850 --> 00:11:38.500
But it starts halfway through.

00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:44.420
That's it!

00:11:45.690 --> 00:11:46.380
Ryuu-kun?

00:11:50.530 --> 00:11:52.260
Oobayashi-kun, right?

00:11:52.280 --> 00:11:56.760
Where were you, at around 9 o'clock, last night.

00:11:57.330 --> 00:11:59.270
I was outside the school.

00:11:59.710 --> 00:12:00.430
With who?

00:12:00.460 --> 00:12:01.640
I was alone.

00:12:01.670 --> 00:12:04.940
I got a message on my cell-phone, with a girls name...

00:12:04.960 --> 00:12:07.480
It said she'd be waiting at a nearby park.

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:10.150
And who was there?

00:12:10.180 --> 00:12:12.200
Well, nobody ever came.

00:12:12.590 --> 00:12:14.200
Don't try and fool us!

00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:15.740
It's true!

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:24.420
Listen, there are only ten people in the school who
don't have alibis for the times of the murders!

00:12:25.110 --> 00:12:28.420
You're also the only one who's strongly connected to the victims!

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:33.800
You were in the same middle school as them...

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:36.640
And you were in the same movie club too, right?

00:12:36.660 --> 00:12:38.100
In other words, you are the criminal!

00:12:38.120 --> 00:12:39.350
Wait, detective.

00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:43.310
It is unlikely that Oobayashi-kun is the perpetrator.

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:45.850
What? You're awfully confident.

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:49.610
Actually, this incident involves a clever trick with alibis.

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:50.690
What?

00:12:51.510 --> 00:13:00.490
I shall now explain how the Collector avoided suspicion,
by using the Internet and an alibi trick.

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:09.200
First, look at this.

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:18.210
This Footage was broadcast over the Internet last night.

00:13:21.990 --> 00:13:23.090
Look closely.

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:28.970
You can tell that she is inviting the criminal into her room.

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:32.930
Oobayashi-kun, this is you, right?

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:35.600
You knew her since middle school.

00:13:35.630 --> 00:13:39.440
So she let you inside without suspecting a thing.

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:40.360
Is that So?

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:46.030
Remember what she said when Kogure Junya was killed?

00:13:46.390 --> 00:13:48.910
"He's got to be the one who did it!"

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:54.540
Would you really let somebody, who you thought
was a murderer, into your room like that?

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:59.670
She wouldn't have acted like this, unless it was a person whom she trusted

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:01.420
to come into her room at night, don't you think?

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:10.310
So when you think about it, her lack of suspicion
here, is proof that Oobayashi is not the criminal.

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:11.720
Right?

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:15.020
Even without that, she always used to hate me.

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:17.060
Then who is the criminal?

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:19.400
We checked all the students without alibis

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:21.570
and he was the only one who was suspicious!

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:24.400
That alibi itself, was the trick.

00:14:25.430 --> 00:14:29.910
Actually, when I saw this footage, the thing I was most interested in was...

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:33.830
This alarm clock.

00:14:35.190 --> 00:14:38.040
Why did they go through all the trouble of showing the alarm clock?

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:43.710
It was because anybody who saw this, would think
that the incident took place in real time.

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:48.380
But, at 8:30 on the night of the murder,

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:51.640
I got a call From her.

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:56.480
At that time, somebody went to her room.

00:14:56.870 --> 00:14:57.810
What?

00:14:58.380 --> 00:15:02.480
Probably, the person who went into her room...

00:15:02.510 --> 00:15:06.860
changed the clock's time when she wasn't looking and then attacked her.

00:15:12.560 --> 00:15:18.540
And then, at 9, broadcast that video over the Internet.

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:21.750
That was the alibi trick that they used.

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:25.920
That does make sense,

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:29.930
but without any proof it's just a crazy theory of yours

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:31.470
We do have proof.

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:31.970
What?

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:35.770
Look at the alarm setting of this clock.

00:15:36.710 --> 00:15:38.600
It's set for just before 9.

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:45.730
School starts at 8:30, why would she set her alarm for 9?

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:49.320
This is the answer.

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:59.750
Actually, just before she was killed, she was trying to
record a video program that she wanted to watch.

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:08.090
This program always starts at 8, doesn't it?

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:13.090
Yes, the video contains a recording of this
program that starts halfway through.

00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:14.050
What does that mean?

00:16:14.620 --> 00:16:21.020
What she really wanted to tape, was a movie that started at 9.

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:29.110
But the timer on her VCR was broken and so
she couldn't set it to automatically record.

00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:36.990
So she set her alarm for 9 and was going to press the record button then.

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:43.830
But, because the criminal secretly changed the time,

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:47.920
she unknowingly pressed the record button earlier than that.

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:55.680
In other words, this is proof that by changing her clock,

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:59.930
the criminal wanted the murder to look like it took place
in real time, therefore, giving themselves an alibi.

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:04.650
So an alibi for 9.00 means nothing.

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:12.150
OK, let's recheck everyone's alibis!

00:17:13.680 --> 00:17:17.950
Detective, may I check the contents of the videos in Asabuki-san's room?

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:26.380
Give it a try, Mr. Detective.

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:31.420
That detective doesn't seem like a bad guy.

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:32.380
Yeah.

00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:38.140
There are a lot of videos here.

00:17:39.540 --> 00:17:40.140
What's wrong?

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:42.350
Those numbered videos...

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:44.310
Number 7 is missing

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:50.400
Do you think that means what she wanted to show us was on that tape?

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:53.280
Let's watch the tapes that are here, starting with number 1.

00:17:58.390 --> 00:18:03.000
This is from the movie club that Asabuki-san said she was in.

00:18:04.230 --> 00:18:06.830
That's Ogura Emina, who went missing!

00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:11.000
And that is the Residence Hall Director Sakuma and Murasaki-sensei.

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:14.010
They look like they are the club president and advisor.

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:17.090
That's Kogure-kun and Asabuki-san.

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:22.890
Oobayashi-kun and Tominaga-kun and Touya-san.

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:26.270
They were all members of the movie club.

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:29.480
Looks like we have narrowed down the range of suspects.

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:39.490
Hey, is the criminal really one of them?

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:41.990
That brings back memories.

00:18:42.020 --> 00:18:45.330
Well, some of us have changed a lot since then.

00:18:46.230 --> 00:18:47.500
Are you talking about me?

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:48.710
Stop it!

00:18:48.730 --> 00:18:49.830
Why?

00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:52.000
We were all friends back then.

00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:57.880
Once you get to high school, you all become rivals.

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:00.350
That was fun.

00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:06.600
We used to watch the movies we made, at
Sakuma-senpai's dad's movie theater.

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:11.770
Or have my father, who worked in the prop business, show us sets.

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:14.900
More importantly, let's think about the murder.

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:17.070
That's why we're here, right?

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:23.280
Thanks for helping me out back there, Amakusa.

00:19:23.310 --> 00:19:24.740
That was amazing!

00:19:24.980 --> 00:19:29.830
Yeah, to think the clock on the video was set 30 minutes ahead.

00:19:30.310 --> 00:19:34.300
Or that the clock was set for night, not morning.

00:19:35.530 --> 00:19:37.630
By the way, I'd like to ask...

00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:41.590
Do you know what was on the tape that came after this one?

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:43.050
Dunno.

00:19:43.080 --> 00:19:45.770
It was a long time ago and this is the first time I've seen these tapes.

00:19:46.210 --> 00:19:48.640
If you remember anything, let me know.

00:19:49.210 --> 00:19:50.980
But who do you suppose did it?

00:19:58.510 --> 00:20:02.530
It looks like seeing these video tapes was pretty hard on the criminal.

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:04.490
He cracked just a bit.

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:05.740
Just now?

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:07.870
Yeah. I've got an idea who did it.

00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:12.380
All we need now is a motive and to disprove his alibi for Kogure Junya's death.

00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:16.000
What?

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:19.260
What's this?

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:26.260
“Anime, I hate you.

00:20:26.290 --> 00:20:28.270
"Anime, die." Huh?

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:30.140
Kogure-kun wrote all these?

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:40.490
But they are all different names.

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:47.160
On the Internet, one person can easily pretend
to be many, by using different handles.

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:50.160
Anyway, read the last one.

00:20:50.690 --> 00:20:51.250
The last one?

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:57.000
"To the many of you who hate me,"

00:20:57.030 --> 00:20:58.380
"this is my last message"

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:01.420
"I'm going to kill myself."

00:21:04.330 --> 00:21:04.970
No way!

00:21:05.370 --> 00:21:07.470
To kill yourself because of online abuse?

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:08.720
It's not impossible.

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:13.350
There are people who fall in love and marry just
from message board posts made on the Internet.

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:14.600
What?

00:21:15.090 --> 00:21:17.190
Right here where they're insulting "anime"...

00:21:18.260 --> 00:21:21.740
they input it in romanji and forgot to change it to hiragana.

00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:23.490
What of it?

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:26.740
This this "anime" is an anagram,

00:21:27.350 --> 00:21:28.240
Anagram?

00:21:32.190 --> 00:21:34.420
If you type it in backwards...

00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:35.500
Look at the romanji.

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:37.170
Emina.

00:21:39.570 --> 00:21:40.260
By Emina you mean...

00:21:42.240 --> 00:21:43.260
Ogura Emina?

00:21:43.910 --> 00:21:47.640
Then the one Kogare-kun was abusing over the Internet, was Ogura Emina?

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:50.220
and she was killed herself?

00:21:50.250 --> 00:21:52.140
It looks like we have got our motive.

00:21:53.420 --> 00:21:55.020
What are you doing?

00:21:55.920 --> 00:21:57.150
Nothing, really.

00:21:57.710 --> 00:22:00.150
Only authorized persons are allowed in here.

00:22:00.170 --> 00:22:01.990
Well, I'm not exactly authorized, but...

00:22:02.010 --> 00:22:02.570
What?

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:04.650
I've heard that voice somewhere.

00:22:05.470 --> 00:22:06.610
Come with me.

00:22:08.350 --> 00:22:09.740
I'm not a suspicious person!

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:11.620
Kyuu!

00:22:11.680 --> 00:22:12.200
Megu!

00:22:12.230 --> 00:22:13.000
Ryuu!

00:22:13.020 --> 00:22:13.830
What?

00:22:13.850 --> 00:22:14.960
You know him?

00:22:16.270 --> 00:22:20.130
I heard that this crime was getting really big so I just...

00:22:21.240 --> 00:22:21.920
You came?

00:22:24.950 --> 00:22:27.470
This is the place Kogure was killed?

00:22:28.620 --> 00:22:33.930
It's quite likely that the criminal also used an alibi trick here.

00:22:34.580 --> 00:22:36.560
But I don't know what kind of trick yet.

00:22:37.250 --> 00:22:38.560
Anyway, let's go in.

00:22:40.630 --> 00:22:41.900
Keep up the good work!

00:22:41.920 --> 00:22:42.900
Hey!

00:22:44.430 --> 00:22:46.240
What do you mean "keep up the good work"?

00:22:46.260 --> 00:22:47.450
This place is off-limits!

00:22:48.470 --> 00:22:51.200
They aren't going to let us in easily, are they?

00:22:53.060 --> 00:22:56.830
I'm jealous of these ants, they can go in and out as they please.

00:22:57.190 --> 00:22:57.620
Ants?

00:23:06.030 --> 00:23:06.840
You're right.

00:23:07.200 --> 00:23:08.890
But why are there so many coming out of an uninhabited building?

00:23:27.550 --> 00:23:28.400
I get it!

00:23:28.720 --> 00:23:29.860
Ryuu, that's...

00:23:30.350 --> 00:23:33.200
The trick used in Kogure Junya's murder!

00:23:45.590 --> 00:23:47.420
THOSE THINGS REFLECTED IN YOUR EYES...

00:23:47.420 --> 00:23:49.760
...ARE DESTINED TO FALL APART.

00:23:49.760 --> 00:23:52.430
NO! NO! NO! NO! BELIEVING IN THAT...

00:23:52.430 --> 00:23:54.090
...IS UP TO YOU.

00:23:54.090 --> 00:23:56.100
LOVE AND KINDNESS...

00:23:56.100 --> 00:23:58.390
...OFTEN STEM FROM SELFISHNESS.

00:23:58.390 --> 00:24:00.930
IF YOU STILL PURSUE THEM...

00:24:00.930 --> 00:24:02.730
...YOU'RE JUST WANDERING AIMLESSLY.

00:24:03.440 --> 00:24:06.980
IT CAN SEEM BOTH FAR AND NEAR...

00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:10.610
THAT PLACE WHERE LOVE LIVES.

00:24:11.650 --> 00:24:13.700
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:13.700 --> 00:24:16.120
...IS A MESSAGE TO YOU.

00:24:16.120 --> 00:24:18.240
YOU'RE USED TO WAITING FOR IT...

00:24:18.240 --> 00:24:19.790
...WITHOUT GIVING UP!

00:24:20.250 --> 00:24:22.460
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:22.460 --> 00:24:24.670
EVEN WHEN WE'RE LOST...

00:24:25.170 --> 00:24:26.880
...CAN'T WE BELIEVE...

00:24:26.880 --> 00:24:30.380
...THAT WE CAN STILL DO IT?

00:24:31.170 --> 00:24:33.340
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:33.340 --> 00:24:35.260
EVEN WHEN WERE LOST...

00:24:35.260 --> 00:24:37.640
...CAN'T WE BELIEVE...

00:24:37.680 --> 00:24:40.470
...THAT WE CAN STILL DO?

00:24:47.740 --> 00:24:56.470
Next Episode

00:24:47.900 --> 00:24:50.470
Ryuu discovers the alibi trick used in Asabuki's murder

00:24:50.490 --> 00:24:52.430
and the crime begins to unravel.

00:24:53.160 --> 00:24:54.850
The motive is made clear

00:24:54.870 --> 00:24:57.390
and the surprising true identity of the Collector is revealed.

00:24:57.870 --> 00:25:06.530
After this, Do you like uniforms?

00:24:58.080 --> 00:25:00.020
On the run, the criminal counterattacks.

00:25:00.380 --> 00:25:03.690
Can the Q Class stop their rampage?

00:25:07.590 --> 00:25:08.360
By the way Megu?

00:25:08.760 --> 00:25:09.530
What is it, Kyuu?

00:25:10.140 --> 00:25:11.860
Is that the school's uniform?

00:25:12.550 --> 00:25:13.740
Yeah, why?

00:25:15.770 --> 00:25:16.660
What?

00:25:17.480 --> 00:25:18.500
Is something weird about it?

00:25:18.850 --> 00:25:20.290
Yeah, it doesn't look like you.

00:25:21.290 --> 00:25:21.970
Kid
